# All files ignore
*

# White lists
# A directory line (ending in /) only lets git look inside that directory: `*`
# still ignores every file in it, so each file needs its own line. Without the
# directory line, git never looks inside and the file lines have no effect.
# A new file stays ignored until it gets its own line, so nothing slips in via
# `git add -A`.
